From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:09:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ACPI: platform_profile: Do not use acpi_kobj after a failed
 ACPI init

Brandon Williams's change that lets platform_profile register without
ACPI (part of the Surface Pro 11 platform support) uses the legacy
/sys/firmware/acpi/platform_profile interface whenever acpi_kobj is set.
That is not enough: if acpi_bus_init() fails, acpi_init() calls
kobject_put(acpi_kobj) and disable_acpi() but leaves acpi_kobj pointing
at the released kobject. The acpi_disabled check that his change
removed from platform_profile_init() kept this driver away from
it. Armin Wolf's 2025 patch for non-ACPI platforms [1] has the same gap.

Use the legacy interface only when ACPI is enabled and acpi_kobj is
set. Devicetree systems, where acpi_disabled is set and acpi_kobj is
NULL, and systems where ACPI initialized normally behave as before.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20250518185111.3560-1-W_Armin@gmx.de [1]
Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/acpi/platform_profile.c | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/platform_profile.c b/drivers/acpi/platform_profile.c
index f120fa60f0d..625136bda18 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/platform_profile.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/platform_profile.c
@@ -48,10 +48,19 @@ static DEFINE_IDA(platform_profile_ida);
  * The per-device class interface is firmware agnostic. Keep the legacy
  * aggregate interface under /sys/firmware/acpi optional so platform-profile
  * drivers can also be used on device-tree systems.
+ *
+ * acpi_kobj alone does not show whether the legacy interface is usable:
+ * if the ACPI bus fails to initialize, acpi_init() releases the kobject
+ * and disables ACPI but does not clear the pointer.
  */
+static bool platform_profile_legacy_available(void)
+{
+	return !acpi_disabled && acpi_kobj;
+}
+
 static void platform_profile_legacy_notify(void)
 {
-	if (acpi_kobj)
+	if (platform_profile_legacy_available())
 		sysfs_notify(acpi_kobj, NULL, "platform_profile");
 }
 
@@ -618,7 +627,7 @@ struct device *platform_profile_register(struct device *dev, const char *name,
 
 	platform_profile_legacy_notify();
 
-	if (acpi_kobj) {
+	if (platform_profile_legacy_available()) {
 		err = sysfs_update_group(acpi_kobj, &platform_profile_group);
 		if (err)
 			goto cleanup_cur;
@@ -655,7 +664,7 @@ void platform_profile_remove(struct device *dev)
 	device_unregister(&pprof->dev);
 
 	platform_profile_legacy_notify();
-	if (acpi_kobj)
+	if (platform_profile_legacy_available())
 		sysfs_update_group(acpi_kobj, &platform_profile_group);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(platform_profile_remove);
@@ -708,7 +717,7 @@ static int __init platform_profile_init(void)
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	if (!acpi_kobj)
+	if (!platform_profile_legacy_available())
 		return 0;
 
 	err = sysfs_create_group(acpi_kobj, &platform_profile_group);
@@ -720,7 +729,7 @@ static int __init platform_profile_init(void)
 
 static void __exit platform_profile_exit(void)
 {
-	if (acpi_kobj)
+	if (platform_profile_legacy_available())
 		sysfs_remove_group(acpi_kobj, &platform_profile_group);
 	class_unregister(&platform_profile_class);
 }
-- 
